   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>Read a matrix in zigzag order along its diagonals, the way some picture formats store their pixels. Number the diagonals by <code>d = i + j</code> (row index plus column index, both from 0), and visit <code>d = 0, 1, 2, …</code> in turn. On a diagonal with odd <code>d</code> walk from its top-right end down to its bottom-left end; on a diagonal with even <code>d</code> walk from its bottom-left end up to its top-right end.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code> and <code>m</code>. Each of the next <code>n</code> lines holds <code>m</code> integers.</p>",
   "output": "<p>All <code>n · m</code> numbers on one line in zigzag order, separated by single spaces.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n, m ≤ 30; every number is between −1000 and 1000.</p>",
