   "hint": "<p>On diagonal <code>d</code> the row <code>i</code> goes from <code>max(0, d − (m − 1))</code> to <code>min(d, n − 1)</code>, and the column is <code>d − i</code>. Collect that diagonal, then reverse it when needed.</p>",
   "solution": "n, m = map(int, input().split())\na = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(n)]\nout = []\nfor d in range(n + m - 1):\n    diag = []\n    for i in range(max(0, d - (m - 1)), min(d, n - 1) + 1):\n        diag.append(a[i][d - i])\n    if d % 2 == 0:\n        diag.reverse()\n    out += diag\nprint(*out)",
