   "title": "The Game of Life",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>In the Game of Life every cell of a grid is alive (<code>#</code>) or dead (<code>.</code>). Each step, all cells change at the same moment, looking at their 8 neighbours (sides and corners; cells outside the grid count as dead):</p><ul><li>a live cell with 2 or 3 live neighbours stays alive, otherwise it dies;</li><li>a dead cell with exactly 3 live neighbours comes alive, otherwise it stays dead.</li></ul><p>Show the grid after <code>k</code> steps.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>, <code>m</code> and <code>k</code>. Each of the next <code>n</code> lines holds <code>m</code> characters, each <code>#</code> or <code>.</code>.</p>",
   "output": "<p>The grid after <code>k</code> steps: <code>n</code> lines of <code>m</code> characters.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n, m ≤ 25; 1 ≤ k ≤ 10.</p>",
   "examples": [
    {
     "in": "5 5 1\n.....\n..#..\n..#..\n..#..\n.....\n",
     "out": ".....\n.....\n.###.\n.....\n.....\n",
     "why": "A line of three cells flips between standing up and lying down."
    }
   ],
   "hint": "<p>Build a brand-new grid for the next step from the old one. Updating the old grid in place would make some cells see their neighbours' <em>new</em> states.</p>",
   "solution": "n, m, k = map(int, input().split())\ng = [input() for _ in range(n)]\nfor _ in range(k):\n    new = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        line = ''\n        for j in range(m):\n            alive = 0\n            for di in (-1, 0, 1):\n                for dj in (-1, 0, 1):\n                    if di == 0 and dj == 0:\n                        continue\n                    r, c = i + di, j + dj\n                    if 0 <= r < n and 0 <= c < m and g[r][c] == '#':\n                        alive += 1\n            if g[i][j] == '#':\n                line += '#' if alive in (2, 3) else '.'\n            else:\n                line += '#' if alive == 3 else '.'\n        new.append(line)\n    g = new\nfor line in g:\n    print(line)",
