   "slug": "magic-square",
   "title": "Is It Magic?",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>An <code>n × n</code> grid is a <em>magic square</em> if it holds each of the numbers 1, 2, …, <code>n²</code> exactly once, and every row, every column and both diagonals add up to the same total. Decide whether the given grid is a magic square.</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>. Each of the next <code>n</code> lines holds <code>n</code> integers.</p>",
   "output": "<p><code>YES</code> or <code>NO</code>.</p>",
   "constraints": "<p>1 ≤ n ≤ 15; every number is between 0 and 1000.</p>",
