   "title": "Turned or Not?",
   "level": 3,
   "statement": "<p>Two square matrices <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> of the same size are given. Can <code>B</code> be made by turning <code>A</code> clockwise by 0°, 90°, 180° or 270°? Print the smallest such angle, or <code>-1</code> if no turn works. (A mirror image is not a turn.)</p>",
   "input": "<p>The first line holds <code>n</code>. The next <code>n</code> lines hold <code>A</code>, and the <code>n</code> lines after that hold <code>B</code>.</p>",
   "output": "<p>One of <code>0</code>, <code>90</code>, <code>180</code>, <code>270</code> or <code>-1</code>.</p>",
